# sysutils_groups (Data Source)

{{ .Description | trimspace }}

The data source parses `/etc/group` with the same code as the [`sysutils_group`](./group.md) data source and the [`sysutils_group`](../resources/group.md) resource. Groups provided only by directory services such as LDAP or SSSD are not listed. Blank lines, comments and NIS compat entries (lines starting with `+` or `-`) are skipped. The data source does not require root privileges.

All filters are optional and combine with AND; without any, every entry is returned. An empty result is not an error.

The data source is read during planning, so groups that [`sysutils_group`](../resources/group.md) resources in the same configuration create are only listed if the data source depends on them, for example with `depends_on`.

